  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2020-07-24T17:25:12.057Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "With the new jump button mapped for Oculus, users can no longer rotate their viewpoint and jump at the same time. Having Jump set to clicking the analog stick, as it has been, has allowed for constant control over gestures, jumping, and camera rotation. Having Jump set to the A button, while making sense in a general video game context, is taking control away from the player. Not to mention many Oculus users use the unused face buttons for Playspacemover, but that's not a \"You\" problem, since it's not provided by you. \nI'd love for and suggest the jump to remain tied to clicking in the Right Stick, Hand Menu tied to pressing B, and Radial Menu tied to Holding B. Thank you for your time.",
